		"howto.day.title": "Day",
		"howto.day.text": "People live in the village, and vampires live among them. They look like everyone else and don't know each other. You are a villager with a lantern.\n\nBy day everyone is on the square. Tap a villager: accuse them, invite them to spend the night together, ask where they sleep, or promise to open the door. Hold your finger on a villager to show with a gesture whether you trust them.\n\nTap a job icon: water, firewood, lamps. The more supplies, the brighter and safer the night.",
		"howto.night.title": "Night",
		"howto.night.text": "In the evening the bell rings and everyone runs home. While it rings, tap a house. There are fewer shelters than people: whoever stays outside will hardly see the morning.\n\nBeing alone in a house is dangerous too: the charm goes out. In the day, agree on who you'll sleep with. If you haven't picked a house, you run to the one you planned and arrive last.",
		"howto.door.title": "The door",
		"howto.door.text": "Whoever reaches a house first decides who gets in. The visitor pleads through the door. Ask \"Who's there?\" or inspect them: you can inspect two visitors a night, but a sign can mislead. Tap the candle to change its flame: brighter shows more, but the thing outside presses harder.\n\nLet in a vampire and you won't see the morning. Let in nobody and you're alone. The Mimic knocks with the voice of someone who isn't here: don't open.\n\nIn the morning, check who slept where and who lied.",
		"howto.talisman.title": "The charm",
		"howto.talisman.text": "Every house has a charm. It holds back the thing from the forest. One person can't hold a charm until morning, so in the day agree on who you'll sleep with.\n\nSwipe over the charm at the door to check it. In the day you can fix it: that's a job on the square. Oil from a night visitor and chalk from the box also strengthen it.",
		"howto.marks.title": "Marks",
		"howto.marks.text": "Marks over a villager's head show what the village knows about them. They are clues and can be wrong: people lie out of fear too. The \"?\" button on the day screen explains each mark and shows what is known about you.",
		"howto.jobs.title": "Jobs and the box",
		"howto.jobs.text": "Tap a job icon on the square and your hero gets to work: water, firewood, lamps, fish, the charm. Full supplies lower the chance of dying at night and light the lamps.\n\nVampires pretend to work or even spoil what's done. Those seen at a spoiled job get marked.\n\nSometimes a box appears at the edge of the square. Whoever opens it first gets what's inside: a note about two villagers, one of them a vampire (only you see it), lamp oil or chalk for a charm.",
		"howto.events.title": "Special nights",
		"howto.events.text": "Nights differ. Fog, a full moon, heavy rain and a quiet night change the rules.\n\nThere may be a hatch behind a house. You can crawl through the tunnel into another house if it has room, but in the morning everyone learns where you came from.",
		"howto.roles.title": "Roles and the meeting",
		"howto.roles.text": "Some people have a role, known only to them. The Elder looks at someone's drawings once a game and learns whether they are a vampire. The Healer takes herbs before the night and saves whoever is attacked in the same house. The Headman's vote counts double when banishing.\n\nFrom day two, the village votes in the evening on who to banish. The banished leave for good; who they were is revealed at the end. Once a game you can ring the bell (\"Meeting!\") and call the vote early.\n\nThe Diary records who slept where, who lied and who promised what. The Log keeps the day's events.",
		"howto.campaign.title": "Campaign and modes",
		"howto.campaign.text": "The campaign has 12 chapters in four acts, from summer to spring. A chapter's goal and two extra goals give up to three stars. Those who die for good don't come back, and the living remember who opened the door for them and who broke a promise. You can replay a finished chapter with the \"Replay\" button: stars can go up, but the village's story stays as it was.\n\nThere is also a quick game against bots on three difficulty levels, the daily challenge (one try a day, with a streak), the Village book (villagers, endings, achievements, comics) and \"Look\": appearance, lantern and hat. They unlock with wins and don't affect play.",
		"howto.more": "Read about the charm, marks, roles and the campaign later: menu, \"How to play\".",
		"howto.title": "How to play · {a} of {b}",
