		"ach.saved_bond.desc": "Let someone you admit and a person close to them both survive the match.",
		"camp.a2c1.title": "The Ford",
		"camp.a2c1.desc": "The village has reached the mill. It has rained for three days, the lamps keep going out, and the miller doesn't let everyone in.",
		"camp.a2c1.beat1_title": "Chapter 4. The Ford",
		"camp.a2c1.beat1": "The miller opened the gate only by evening. He says refugees were here before you. Where they are now, he won't say.",
		"camp.a2c1.beat2_title": "Rain",
		"camp.a2c1.beat2": "The rain hasn't stopped for three days. Lamps go out, and you reach the door by feel, along slippery boards.",
		"camp.a2c2.title": "Strangers",
		"camp.a2c2.desc": "Strangers come off the road. Nobody knows what they became on the way.",
		"camp.a2c2.beat1_title": "Chapter 5. Strangers",
		"camp.a2c2.beat1": "Strangers came to the mill from the road. The miller let them into the yard and locked the gate from outside. Just in case.",
		"camp.a2c2.beat2_title": "Three mornings",
		"camp.a2c2.beat2": "Every morning you learn something new about the strangers. By the third morning you'll know whom you let in. If you live that long.",
		"camp.a2c3.title": "Flood",
		"camp.a2c3.desc": "The river breaks its banks. Fewer dry places, more people, and a full moon.",
		"camp.a2c3.beat1_title": "Chapter 6. Flood",
		"camp.a2c3.beat1": "At night the river broke its banks. The Dugout is flooded; the Hermitage can only be reached along the boards.",
		"camp.a2c3.beat2_title": "Upriver",
		"camp.a2c3.beat2": "The miller said: whoever lives till morning goes with him upriver, to the monastery. The river will take the rest.",
		"camp.act2.end_all": "Almost everyone goes upriver. The mill wheel stops behind your backs.",
		"camp.act2.end_some": "Only a few go to the monastery. The miller locks the gate and stays by the river.",
		"camp.act2.end_none": "You go to the monastery without those you started with. The river carries away what's left of the mill.",
		"goal.guest_secret": "Learn the strangers' secret to the end",
		"ending.act2_all": "Act II: almost everyone goes upriver",
		"ending.act2_some": "Act II: only a few reach the monastery",
		"ending.act2_none": "Act II: the river takes the mill",
		"ach.act2.name": "Upriver",
		"ach.act2.desc": "Finish Act II of the campaign.",
		"narr.ignat": "Brother Ignat",
		"narr.keeper": "Stationmaster",
		"ach.act3.name": "The Bell Behind You",
		"ach.act3.desc": "Finish Act III of the campaign.",
		"ach.act4.name": "The Last Train",
		"ach.act4.desc": "Finish the whole campaign.",
		"camp.a3c1.title": "The Gate",
		"camp.a3c1.desc": "The monks let you inside the wall but lock the cells for the night. Fog rolls in from the marsh: at the door you'll have to ask.",
		"camp.a3c1.beat1_title": "Chapter 7. The Gate",
		"camp.a3c1.beat1": "Brother Ignat opened the gate only to those who gave their name, and wrote each one into his book. The names of those who came before you have crosses next to them.",
		"camp.a3c1.beat2_title": "Fog",
		"camp.a3c1.beat2": "By nightfall fog rose from the marsh. Over the wall you can only see the lights in the windows. You can't see who's knocking, you can only ask.",
		"camp.a3c2.title": "The Bell",
		"camp.a3c2.desc": "At night the bell rings by itself. Find the vampire before the third morning, before the abbot has the gate locked behind you.",
		"camp.a3c2.beat1_title": "Chapter 8. The Bell",
		"camp.a3c2.beat1": "At midnight someone rang the bell. Brother Ignat swears the bell tower was locked and the key hung round his neck all night.",
		"camp.a3c2.beat2_title": "Silence",
		"camp.a3c2.beat2": "The abbot ordered silence until morning. On nights like this nobody knocks with a stranger's voice, but you can't hear your own people beyond the wall either.",
		"camp.a3c3.title": "The Crypt",
		"camp.a3c3.desc": "Empty coffins under the church. Two vampires, a full moon and five nights until the road to the station.",
		"camp.a3c3.beat1_title": "Chapter 9. The Crypt",
		"camp.a3c3.beat1": "A crypt was found under the church. The coffins are empty and the lids were pushed aside from within. The monks act as if it has always been so.",
		"camp.a3c3.beat2_title": "The Road to the Station",
		"camp.a3c3.beat2": "Brother Ignat knows a path through the forest to the railway. He'll lead only those who survive the full moon.",
		"camp.act3.end_all": "Almost everyone leaves for the station. Brother Ignat shuts the gate behind you and stays to ring the bell.",
		"camp.act3.end_some": "Only a few reach the station. The bell rings after you all the way to the forest.",
		"camp.act3.end_none": "You go to the station without the people you started with. Behind you the monastery is silent.",
		"ending.act3_all": "Act III: almost everyone leaves for the station",
		"ending.act3_some": "Act III: the bell sees off only a few",
		"ending.act3_none": "Act III: the monastery falls silent",
		"camp.a4c1.title": "The Halt",
		"camp.a4c1.desc": "The forest ends at the rails. At the halt there's a stationmaster and an empty station, and they say a train will come in four nights.",
		"camp.a4c1.beat1_title": "Chapter 10. The Halt",
		"camp.a4c1.beat1": "Brother Ignat's path led to the rails. One lantern burns at the halt, and on the stationmaster's desk lies a timetable with a single train.",
		"camp.a4c1.beat2_title": "Rain",
		"camp.a4c1.beat2": "It has rained over the tracks for three days. The lanterns go out, by morning the footprints on the sleepers are washed away, and nobody can tell who went to the wagon at night.",
		"camp.a4c2.title": "The List",
		"camp.a4c2.desc": "The stationmaster is writing a list for the train, and there are fewer seats than people. Find the vampire before the third morning, before the list is closed.",
		"camp.a4c2.beat1_title": "Chapter 11. The List",
		"camp.a4c2.beat1": "The stationmaster took out a notebook: the train has fewer seats than there are of you. He only writes down those that others vouch for.",
		"camp.a4c2.beat2_title": "Fog",
		"camp.a4c2.beat2": "Fog again from the marsh. At night people come to the shelters begging for a place, and you only see who's knocking right at the door.",
		"camp.a4c3.title": "The Last Train",
		"camp.a4c3.desc": "The last nights before the train. Everyone who survived is at one station, and two vampires want to leave with you.",
		"camp.a4c3.beat1_title": "Chapter 12. The Last Train",
		"camp.a4c3.beat1": "The train will come at dawn after the fifth night. The stationmaster says only those who reach the platform on their own will be let into the wagon.",
		"camp.a4c3.beat2_title": "Full Moon",
		"camp.a4c3.beat2": "The moon is full and the forest has come right up to the rails. Tonight decides who goes on with you.",
		"camp.act4.end_all": "The train leaves at dawn. Almost everyone who left the village with you is in the wagon, and the forest outside the window keeps getting smaller.",
		"camp.act4.end_some": "The train leaves at dawn. Only a few of the people you started with are beside you. Nobody takes the empty seats.",
		"camp.act4.end_none": "The train leaves at dawn. You travel alone. All that's left of the village is names in the stationmaster's notebook.",
		"ending.act4_all": "Finale: the train takes almost everyone",
		"ending.act4_some": "Finale: empty seats in the wagon",
		"ending.act4_none": "Finale: you travel alone",
