		"rev.boat.title": "The empty boat",
		"rev.boat.text": "{who} takes you down to the jetty: \"The night they called you from the other bank, the boat came back on its own. Empty, the oar still in place. I never told anyone.\"",
		"rev.boat.item": "By the jetty you find an oar covered in notches: one for every night the boat came back empty. The last notch is fresh, from the night they called you from the other bank.",
		"rev.board.title": "Names on the board",
		"rev.board.text": "{who} shows you the board by the chapel: \"These are the ones who went to the river and never came back. One name was carved thirty years ago, and nobody remembers who it was.\"",
		"rev.board.item": "In an abandoned notebook you find the list of names from the chapel board. One name is circled, with a note beside it: \"thirty years ago\".",
		"rev.grave.title": "A fresh grave",
		"rev.grave.text": "{who} meets you at the mill gate: \"There's a fresh grave behind the mill, no name on it. Dug this week. The miller says he doesn't know whose.\"",
		"rev.grave.item": "A spade caked in wet clay leans by the mill gate, and behind the shed there's a mound of fresh earth with no cross and no name.",
		"ph.PROMISE_BOT_OPEN": ["If you knock at my door tonight, I'll open. You have my word.", "Knock at my place tonight. I'll let you in.", "Listen, come to my door tonight and it'll be open. I promise."],
		"ph.PROMISE_REPLY_OPEN": ["I'll remember that. I'll knock three times.", "All right. Just don't change your mind when you hear the knock.", "I'm holding you to that."],
		"ph.PROMISE_REPLY_COME": ["I'll be waiting. Knock loud, I sleep deep.", "Come. It's less scary with two.", "All right. If nobody comes, I'll know something happened."],
		"ph.PROMISE_KEPT_OPEN": ["You kept your word. I won't forget it.", "Thanks for the door. I didn't think anyone would open.", "A promise is a promise. Thank you."],
		"ph.PROMISE_KEPT_COME": ["You kept your word. The night was easier with two.", "The night is shorter with two. Thanks for keeping your word."],
		"ph.PROMISE_BROKEN_OPEN": ["You gave your word: you'd open if I knocked. I knocked twice.", "You promised to open the door. Remember? I stood on that step till the end.", "I trusted your word. I won't again."],
		"ph.PROMISE_BROKEN_COME": ["I waited all night. You said you'd come. Nobody came.", "You promised to sleep at my place. I listened for footsteps until dawn."],
		## Группы 2–3 плана: чувства, связи, реакции на утрату, сцены главы «Стук» (TASK-006–015)
		"feel.grief": "Grieving for {lost}.",
