		"memo.react_revenge": "{who} said nothing. That's worse.",
		## Группа 4 плана: туман, улики, пустая лодка, имя на доске, прощание (TASK-016–020)
		"clue.title": "Clue notebook",
		"clue.btn": "Clues ({n})",
		"clue.hint": "Pick two entries. If they contradict each other, ask that person in front of everyone.",
		"clue.none": "Nothing to write down yet. Listen to who promised to sleep where, and watch who knocks at night.",
		"clue.day": "day {n}",
		"clue.claim": "{who.cap} said {who:he|she|you} would sleep in {house.in}.",
		"clue.seen": "At night {who} knocked at {house}.",
		"clue.say_home": "{who.cap} says {who:he|she|you} stayed home all night and never went out.",
		"clue.find_tracks": "Fresh tracks by the jetty match {who}'s boots. Someone walked to the boat in them at night.",
		"clue.boat_oar": "The boat is tied with its bow toward the village, not the way it was yesterday. The oar is wet.",
		"clue.boat_scarf": "A stranger's scarf lies in the bottom of the boat. It's dry, though the boat sat on the water all night.",
		"clue.no_conflict": "These entries don't contradict each other.",
		"clue.conflict": "These entries contradict each other. You can ask in front of everyone.",
		"clue.ask": "Ask in front of everyone",
		"clue.token": "Contradiction confirmed. Question tokens: {n}.",
		"clue.asked": "This was already asked.",
		"say.confront": "{who}, I have one thing written down and something else happened. Explain, in front of everyone.",
		"ph.CLUE_ADMIT": ["Fine. I went to the river to check the boat. Couldn't sleep.", "Yes, I lied. I was afraid you'd suspect me.", "It's true. Someone called from the other bank, I went to look. Nobody there."],
		"ph.CLUE_DENY": ["Nothing like that happened. You're mixing things up.", "Who do you trust, me or tracks in the mud?", "I was home. Enough."],
		"ph.MEM_WRONG": ["Of course I remember. Open up, I'll tell you later.", "That talk? Yes, yes. Open up, it's cold.", "We had a deal. Open up."],
		"door.mem_ask": "What did we talk about?",
		"door.mem_story": "\"Today we talked about this: {text}.\"",
		"door.mem_promise": "\"We made a deal today. I remember my word.\"",
		"door.mem_ok": "The voice remembers what only the two of you knew.",
		"door.mem_bad": "The voice dodges the question. The one you talked to today would remember.",
		"door.fog_voice": "A voice from the fog",
		"door.fog_claim": "Says it's {me}",
		"fog.teach": "The fog is here. In fog a voice can be faked, memory can't. At the door, ask about what only the two of you know.",
		"fog.widow": "My husband walked into a fog like this. I knew his voice and opened. It wasn't him.",
		"sc.board.1": "Look at the bottom line. I've been washing this board for thirty years and only noticed now.",
		"sc.board.2": "On the chapel board, under the names of those who went to the river, someone carved: \"{name}\". The letters are old and dark.",
		"sc.board.2_noname": "On the chapel board, under the names of those who went to the river, someone carved your name. The letters are old and dark.",
		"sc.board.3": "Thirty years ago someone with this name was already here. Tell me straight: is it you?",
		"sc.board.alone": "Nobody at the chapel. On the board of those who went to the river there are fresh shavings: someone cleaned the bottom line.",
		"sc.board.ask": "What do you say?",
		"sc.board.c_confess": "\"That's my name. I remember this river.\"",
		"sc.board.c_deny": "\"A coincidence. It's a common name.\"",
		"sc.board.c_silent": "Say nothing",
		"sc.board.r_confess": "So the river let you go, and now it's calling you back. I won't tell anyone. For now.",
		"sc.board.r_deny": "Fine, a coincidence. I'm calmer that way.",
		"sc.board.r_silent": "You're silent. Then I decide what that means.",
		"day.p_send": "Send across the river by boat",
		"day.send_ask": "At dawn {who} will cross the river and won't come back this chapter. If the river takes {who:him|her|you}. Send?",
		"day.send_yes": "Send",
		"sys.send": "At dawn {who} will cross the river.",
		"log.sent": "{who.cap} crossed the river.",
		"log.sent_back": "{who.cap} came back: the boat turned around midstream.",
		"mo.sent": "{who.cap} left at dawn. The boat is already at the far bank, empty.",
		"mo.sent_back": "{who.cap} is back on the jetty: the boat turned around by itself midstream. The river doesn't take everyone.",
		"farewell.warm": "Thank you. If I come back, I'll knock three times.",
		"farewell.cold": "You want to be rid of me. Fine, I'll go.",
		"rev.boat_answer.title": "Who brought the boat",
		"rev.boat_answer.text": "{who} stares at the water for a long time: \"Nobody stole the boat. The one who called you from the other bank kept bringing it. He waited for someone here to take it. He's still waiting.\"",
		"rev.boat_answer.item": "The oar, the scarf and the tracks by the jetty add up: the boat was brought from the other bank. The one who called you by name is still waiting.",
		"camp.act1.boat": "The empty boat is explained: it was brought from the other bank.",
		"camp.act1.boat_open": "Who kept bringing the empty boat is still unknown.",
		"camp.act1.board_confess": "The name on the board is yours now, and the village knows it.",
		"camp.act1.board_deny": "The name on the board stayed a stranger's. For now.",
		"camp.act1.board_silent": "The name on the board is still unanswered.",
		## Группа 5 плана: мельник, его тайна, чужаки, половодье, память акта I (TASK-021–025)
		"npc.miller.name": "Savely the miller",
		"npc.line": "{name}: \"{text}\"",
		"npc.busy": "{name} has already answered today. Ask again tomorrow.",
		"npc.miller.q_ford": "What about the ford?",
		"npc.miller.q_before": "Who was here before us?",
		"npc.miller.q_night": "Who knocks at night?",
		"npc.miller.a_ford": "The water is low, knee-deep. But at night it's not people who walk the ford. Lock your doors.",
		"npc.miller.a_before": "Refugees. They stayed a while and went upriver. Not all of them got there, I'd guess.",
		"npc.miller.a_before_known": "Someone's been looking in my book, I see. Yes, they paid. Whoever paid got in. Don't ask more.",
		"npc.miller.a_night": "Nobody comes from the far bank, the water holds the ford at night. Only your own knock. Or those pretending to be.",
		"npc.miller.rule": "I have one rule: at night the ford is closed, knocks come only from this bank. If you don't know them, don't let them in.",
		"npc.miller.board_confess": "They say your name is carved on the chapel board. So you're from there. I'll keep that in mind.",
		"npc.miller.board_deny": "I heard about the chapel board. They say you call it a coincidence. Sure.",
		"npc.miller.board_silent": "They say you had nothing to say about the chapel board. I keep quiet about plenty too.",
		"npc.miller.strangers": "Strangers came in from the road. I let them into the yard. Who they are, you sort out yourselves.",
		"npc.miller.flood": "The river is rising. One more night and the water will reach the low houses.",
		"npc.miller.after_tell": "So it's all out. Well. I won't open the gates for anyone again.",
		"npc.miller.after_keep": "Thank you. I won't forget it. When you go to the monastery, I'll help with the charms.",
		"clue.miller_book": "In the miller's shed, a ledger of payments. A sum next to every name, and next to the last one only a cross.",
		"clue.miller_sack": "An extra sack of flour in the mill yard. The miller told the refugees there was no flour.",
		"clue.miller_lock": "The miller's storeroom is chained shut. Something inside scratches quietly at the boards.",
		"sc.grave.1": "The earth is fresh. I dug every grave here. Not this one.",
		"sc.grave.1_other": "Timur isn't with us, and there's a fresh grave behind the mill. Someone dug it without him.",
		"sc.grave.knife": "In the loose earth, a branded hunting knife. {who} carries one just like it.",
		"sc.grave.stranger": "A stranger in a travelling cloak lies in the grave. Nobody in the village knows him.",
		"sc.grave.blame": "The strangers brought a dead man with them. {who.cap} showed up yesterday, and here we are.",
		"sc.flood.1": "Overnight the river rose by a forearm. The water is already at the low houses.",
		"sc.flood.2": "There's one boat. I can get it to one house and we'll sandbag the door. The other will flood. Where do I take it?",
		"sc.flood.ask": "Where does the boat go?",
		"sc.flood.c_house": "To {house}",
		"sc.miller.1": "At night the miller comes to your door himself. He holds the storeroom key.",
		"sc.miller.1_known": "The ledger, the extra sack, the chain on the storeroom. At night you knock on the miller's door.",
		"sc.miller.2": "I had a daughter. She crossed the river. That night I knew her voice and opened. It wasn't her.",
		"sc.miller.3": "Since then I let people in for pay. The money goes on candles for her. Whoever I turned away, the river took. Wouldn't you have opened?",
		"sc.miller.ask": "What will you do?",
		"sc.miller.c_tell": "Tell the refugees",
		"sc.miller.c_keep": "Keep quiet",
		"log.flood": "Water flooded {house}. Nobody sleeps there for the rest of the chapter; the other houses are more crowded.",
		"night.flooded": "Flooded",
		"ph.PLEA_FLOOD": ["We're flooded. Knee-deep water, let me in, even just onto a bench.", "There's water in {house.in}. I have nowhere else to go.", "I'm soaked, I know. Let me in, the water keeps rising."],
		"carry.react_revenge": "I haven't forgotten anything. And I won't.",
		"carry.react_accuse": "I said in front of everyone it was because of your door. I'll say it here too.",
		"carry.react_defend": "I stood up for you when everyone was shouting. Don't make me regret it.",
		"carry.react_withdraw": "I went quiet back then. I talk again now. Just not to you.",
		"carry.refused_died": "We both remember who didn't open the door that night.",
		"carry.broken": "I was promised the door would open. It didn't. I survived, but I remember.",
		"carry.exiled_by_you": "Your vote decided who was driven out back then. Vote carefully here.",
		"carry.broke_you": "I made you a promise and broke it. Here I'll keep it.",
		"carry.refused": "Your door stayed shut back then. I survived. Let's not do that again.",
		"carry.refused_you": "I didn't open for you back then. I'm still ashamed.",
		"carry.kept": "Your word held, back at that door. I remember.",
		"carry.admitted": "That night your door opened for me. Here mine is open for you.",
		"carry.listened": "I remember our talk by the well. Hardly anyone cared to listen.",
		"carry.letter": "A letter from {who}: \"{text}\"",
		"carry.miller_tell": "Good that the truth about the miller came out. You're someone I can deal with.",
		"carry.miller_keep": "You know something about the miller and you're keeping quiet. I don't like it.",
		"camp.act2.miller_tell": "The refugees know the truth about the miller, and the mill gates closed behind you for good.",
		"camp.act2.miller_keep": "The miller's secret stayed with you, and so did his help.",
		"camp.act2.sum_few": "Over two acts the village lost {n}. Almost everyone made it.",
		"camp.act2.sum_some": "Over two acts the village lost {n}. More empty places in the line than anyone wanted.",
		"camp.act2.sum_many": "Over two acts the village lost {n}. Few are left of those you started with.",
		## Группа 6 плана: книга у ворот, Игнат и Анфиса, колокол, крипта, доверие (TASK-026–030)
		"npc.ignat.name": "Brother Ignat",
		"npc.anfisa.name": "Sister Anfisa",
		"npc.ignat.q_book": "Show the book at the gate",
		"npc.ignat.q_night": "Who knocks at night?",
		"npc.ignat.q_before": "Who was here before us?",
		"npc.ignat.a_night": "Those written in the book, and those someone forgot to write. The second kind knock louder.",
		"npc.ignat.a_before": "Many. There are crosses by their names now. Not all the crosses are mine.",
		"npc.anfisa.q_crossed": "What is the second book?",
		"npc.anfisa.q_heal": "Do you heal people?",
		"npc.anfisa.q_night": "What should we fear at night?",
		"npc.anfisa.a_crossed_early": "Not here. Brother Ignat is watching. Ask me later, when the bell rings.",
		"npc.anfisa.a_crossed": "It's the book of those who were let in and never came back. Crossed out, not forgotten. I copied what matters into your notebook.",
		"npc.anfisa.a_heal": "I heal what can be healed. Fear can't. You can only wait it out.",
		"npc.anfisa.a_night": "Voices you know. There are no strangers here.",
		"npc.ignat.open_a3c1": "The gates close at sunset. Whoever you write in the book gets in without questions. Write a name, and their sin is yours too.",
		"npc.anfisa.open_a3c1": "If anyone falls ill, bring them to me in the refectory. And don't believe everything written at the gate.",
		"npc.ignat.open_a3c2": "At night the bell rings by itself. The key hangs on my neck, the tower is locked. Count the strokes.",
		"npc.anfisa.open_a3c2": "The bell strikes as many times as the house's number. I've been counting for a long time.",
		"npc.ignat.open_a3c3": "There is a crypt under the church. Whoever goes down comes up changed. Or doesn't come up.",
		"npc.anfisa.open_a3c3": "The crypt holds the answer to what you've been asking since the river. You won't like it.",
		"npc.ignat.day1": "Another night is over. The book remembers who asked for whom.",
		"npc.ignat.day2": "I pray for everyone beyond the wall. And for those inside it too.",
		"npc.ignat.day3": "Soon the road to the station. Not everyone I wrote down will get there.",
		"npc.anfisa.day1": "Someone was crying beyond the wall last night. The voice was familiar. I didn't open.",
		"npc.anfisa.day2": "We're almost out of bandages. Look after each other, there's no one else to.",
		"npc.ignat.vouched": "Written: {who}. Their sin is yours now.",
		"npc.anfisa.after_trial": "The people you once let in stood up for you. That's how it works.",
		"clue.vouch": "In the book at the gate: {me} vouched for {who}.",
		"clue.crossed_book": "In Anfisa's second book, the names of those let in who never came back are crossed out. The miller's daughter is there, and so is your name.",
		"day.p_vouch": "Write in the gate book",
		"vouch.title": "The book at the gate",
		"vouch.rule": "Whoever is written here gets in at night without questions. If it's a vampire, the village's trust in you drops twice as hard.",
		"vouch.row": "day {n} · {me} for {who}",
		"vouch.empty": "Nobody has written anyone yet.",
		"vouch.write": "Write: {who}",
		"vouch.ask": "Write {who} in the book? At night {who:he|she|you} will get in to you without questions.",
		"vouch.yes": "Write",
		"vouch.sys": "You write in the gate book: {who}.",
		"vouch.door": "In the book: gets in without questions",
		"log.trust_zero": "The village stopped listening to you: at the next gathering your vote won't count.",
		"log.bell": "at night the bell struck {n} {n#time|times}.",
		"log.trial_exiled": "by Brother Ignat's word the player was driven out of the monastery.",
		"mo.bell": "At night the bell struck {n} {n#time|times}. House number {n} on the shelter list.",
		"vote.trust_mute": "The village isn't listening to you today: your vote doesn't count.",
		"sc.crossed.1": "Brother Ignat doesn't know I keep it. Everyone who was let in and never came back is here.",
		"sc.crossed.2": "The lines are crossed out, but the names show through. The miller's daughter. Unfamiliar surnames. And at the very bottom: \"{name}\".",
		"sc.crossed.2_noname": "The lines are crossed out, but the names show through. The miller's daughter. Unfamiliar surnames. And at the very bottom, your name.",
		"sc.crossed.3": "Someone let every one of them in. And they all came back to knock at the doors of those who remember them.",
		"sc.crossed.boat": "The boat was brought by the one who called you from the far bank. He brought it for you.",
		"sc.crossed.miller": "The miller opened for his daughter because he knew her voice. Since then he let people in for pay.",
		"sc.crossed.board": "Your name was carved on the chapel board thirty years ago. This river has seen you before; only the river kept the memory.",
		"sc.crypt.1": "It's cold under the church. The candle picks out niches: empty coffins, a name on each.",
		"sc.crypt.2": "Carved on the wall: they come to those who remember and mourn them, and ask to be let in with a voice from that memory.",
		"sc.crypt.3": "They called you from the far bank because someone mourned you too.",
		"sc.crypt.ignat": "You came from the far bank. Nobody comes back from there alive. In the morning we decide what you are.",
		"sc.trial.open": "This person came from the far bank. Let those who know them speak. Then we decide.",
		"sc.trial.relay": "Others speak for {who}: \"{text}\"",
		"sc.trial.nobody": "Nobody steps forward. Neither for nor against.",
		"sc.trial.acquit": "People remember more good than harm from you. Live. But I'll be watching.",
		"sc.trial.convict": "More of them remember harm. Leave through the gate before sunset. That's the decision.",
		"trial.def.admitted": "This person opened the door to me when others didn't.",
		"trial.def.kept": "This person promised me and kept their word. Vampires don't keep their word.",
		"trial.def.listened": "This person listened to me when I was at my worst.",
		"trial.def.react_defend": "I stood up for this person then, and I will now.",
		"trial.def.refused_you": "I didn't open for this person, and they never held it against me.",
		"trial.acc.refused_died": "This person didn't open, and someone died at the door.",
		"trial.acc.refused": "This person left me outside. I remember every minute of that night.",
		"trial.acc.broken": "This person promised to open. They didn't.",
		"trial.acc.exiled_by_you": "This person's vote drove out an innocent.",
		"trial.acc.react_accuse": "I've said it in front of everyone: the trouble came through their door.",
		"trial.acc.react_revenge": "I have nothing to say. Decide for yourselves. I decided long ago.",
		"camp.act3.end_trial": "The monastery gates close behind you. The others will go to the station without you. You hear someone calling you from the far bank.",
		"trial.def.broke_you": "I deceived this person, and they never gave me away.",
		"npc.anfisa.day3": "I've seen how you look at the gate. Don't go there at night.",
		"vouch.done_today": "A name is already written today. You can add another tomorrow.",
		"camp.act3.trial_won": "The trial in the crypt ended in your favour thanks to those who remember your doors.",
		## Группа 7 плана: станция, люди станции, список, последний поезд, финал (TASK-031–035)
		"npc.keeper.name": "Stationmaster",
		"npc.keeper.q_list": "The train list",
		"npc.keeper.q_train": "When will the train come?",
		"npc.keeper.q_night": "Who knocks at night?",
		"npc.keeper.a_list_early": "The list comes right before the train. The clerk will write it, not me. Keep an eye on him.",
		"npc.keeper.a_list_list": "I have the list. See for yourself.",
		"npc.keeper.a_train": "The telegraph has been silent for three days. I have the key, and nobody to answer. The train will come. The question is with whom.",
		"npc.keeper.a_night": "At night the rails are walked by those who didn't live to see the train. They know there are few seats.",
		"npc.keeper.open_a4c1": "This is the last station. No more forest past here, only rails. They promised a train in four nights.",
		"npc.keeper.open_a4c2": "We start the list. There are fewer seats than people. The clerk will write, I will watch.",
		"npc.keeper.open_a4c3": "The train is close. Fewer seats than people on the platform. Write one name a day. And don't trust the signatures.",
		"st.worker.open": "I'll fix the engine. I just need to live until it moves.",
		"st.clerk.open": "Ten seats. Fourteen of you at the station. Can you count?",
		"st.struck": "I've been struck off the list. By your hand. I'll remember that.",
		"st.struck_door": "I opened my door to you. And you strike me off the list.",
		"st.covered": "Thank you. I won't forget this. I really won't.",
		"guest.worker.name": "Stanley",
		"guest.worker.title": "Depot worker, {n}. Fixing the engine",
		"guest.worker.story": "Twenty years at the depot. Knows every bolt of the engine on the siding. Says the machine will run if nobody gives up on it.",
		"guest.worker.clue1": "At night hammering was heard from the depot. In the morning {who} said he slept and heard nothing.",
		"guest.worker.clue2": "In {who}'s toolbox lies a piece of someone else's belt. He says he found it on the tracks.",
		"guest.worker.reveal_h": "{who} fixed the engine at night to finish before the train came. He took the belt from a dead stoker to replace a torn one.",
		"guest.worker.reveal_u": "{who} never fixed the engine. In the firebox they found scraps of clothing from those who went to the depot and never came back.",
		"guest.clerk.name": "Archibald",
		"guest.clerk.title": "Clerk, {n}. Writes the train list",
		"guest.clerk.story": "Served in the district office. Neat handwriting, polite smile. He writes the train list because nobody else can write so fast.",
		"guest.clerk.clue1": "Coins jingle in {who}'s pocket. This morning he bought kerosene from the stationmaster and paid in silver.",
		"guest.clerk.clue2": "In {who}'s draft of the list there are numbers next to some names. He says they're carriage numbers.",
		"guest.clerk.reveal_h": "{who} took money for places on the list. Whoever paid ended up higher. He's not a vampire: he just sold salvation.",
		"guest.clerk.reveal_u": "{who} didn't take money for places on the list. Those who paid him didn't come back from the platform at night.",
		"clue.train": "On the train list: {me} wrote down {who}.",
		"day.p_list_write": "Write on the train list",
		"day.p_list_strike": "Strike off the list",
		"list.title": "Train list · seats: {n}",
		"list.rule": "Each day you can write one name and strike one. A struck name can't go back on. A vampire on the list rides with everyone.",
		"list.row": "{who} · written by {me}",
		"list.row_secret": "{who} · signature illegible",
		"list.empty": "The list is empty so far.",
		"list.write": "Write: {who}",
		"list.strike": "Strike: {who}",
		"list.sys_write": "You write on the train list: {who}.",
		"list.sys_strike": "You strike off the list: {who}.",
		"list.cant": "Not today: the list is full or you've already done that today.",
		"sc.betray.1": "Morning on the platform. Fog lies on the rails. The stationmaster holds the list and stares at one line for a long time.",
		"sc.betray.2": "This line was written at night. I know the handwriting. It's {who}'s.",
		"sc.betray.human": "I wanted to live until the train. I wrote down the one I was afraid of, so it wouldn't touch me. Anyone in my place would have done the same.",
		"sc.betray.upyr": "All this way I was your friend. It wasn't hard. I only needed a seat in the carriage.",
		"sc.betray.clerk": "I was paid. I'm a clerk, I write what I'm paid to write. Who paid makes no difference to me.",
		"sc.betray.ask": "What do you say about {who}?",
		"sc.betray.c_expose": "Tell everyone",
		"sc.betray.c_cover": "Cover for them",
		"sc.final.1": "The last night before the train. The station sleeps. Three knocks at the door, the way they knocked on the first night.",
		"sc.final.voice": "It's me, {who}. Open up. I've been waiting for you on the other bank all this time.",
		"sc.final.voice_self": "Behind the door your own voice calls you by name. The one carved on the chapel board.",
		"sc.final.2": "Far away a train whistles. It will be at the platform before dawn.",
		"sc.act2.1": "Autumn. You wade to the mill with your things held over your heads. The wheel turns for nothing: nobody has brought grain here for a long time.",
		"sc.act2.2": "The miller waits on the planks with a lantern and counts you by heads. He counts twice.",
		"sc.act2.3": "There are strangers' footprints on the bank. They lead to the water and never come back.",
		"sc.act2.end": "The wheel stops. For the first time in days you hear only the river.",
		"sc.act3.1": "Winter arrived before the road did. You walk to the monastery knee-deep in snow and hardly speak.",
		"sc.act3.2": "One lantern burns on the wall. A monk stands beneath it and does not move until you come close.",
		"sc.act3.3": "The bell above your heads is silent. Brother Ignat says it is better that way.",
		"sc.act3.end": "The book is closed. The names stay in it where they were written.",
		"sc.act4.1": "Spring. The snow is gone, and the rails show on the embankment. They shine as if someone walked them yesterday.",
		"sc.act4.2": "The platform is drowning in fog. The stationmaster waits by the only lantern and does not ask where you came from.",
		"sc.act4.3": "The timetable on the wall lists one train. The date is rubbed out.",
		"sc.lights.1": "By morning the fog lies on the tracks. Far inside it two yellow lights come on.",
		"sc.lights.2": "There is no whistle. The lights stay where they are, then go out one by one.",
		"sc.lights.3": "The stationmaster says it is not the train. The train has not come yet.",
		"sc.train.1": "You do not open. The knocking weakens and stops. Until dawn there is only waiting.",
		"sc.train.2": "At dawn the train pulls in. The carriage doors open by themselves.",
		"sc.shore.1": "You slide the bolt back. It is brighter outside the door than such a night should be.",
		"sc.shore.2": "Someone is waiting on the other side. You step over the threshold.",
		"sc.final.ask": "What will you do?",
		"sc.final.c_open": "Open and go",
		"sc.final.c_train": "Don't open, wait for the train",
		"fin.btn": "The last night",
		"fin.final_shore": "You open. On the threshold stands the one who was lost before anyone else. The door closes behind you both. In the morning the train leaves without you, and your footprints on the platform lead to the river.",
		"fin.final_upyr": "The train leaves at dawn. The carriage is crowded and quiet. By the third station, people stop coming out of the last compartment. The vampire from the list is riding with you.",
		"fin.final_many": "The train leaves at dawn. Almost everyone who left the village is in the carriage. The forest outside ends, and nobody knocks anymore.",
		"fin.final_few": "The train leaves at dawn. The carriage has many empty seats. You remember who should be sitting in them.",
		"ending.final_shore": "Finale: to the other bank",
		"ending.final_upyr": "Finale: a train with a vampire",
		"ending.final_many": "Finale: almost everyone left",
		"ending.final_few": "Finale: empty seats",
		"fin.epi.dead": "{who} didn't live to see the train.",
		"fin.epi.left_behind": "{who} boarded the train without you.",
		"fin.epi.upyr_car": "{who} is in the last compartment. The door is locked from the inside.",
		"fin.epi.train": "{who} is in the carriage, looking out the window in silence.",
		"fin.epi.station": "{who} stayed at the station. The next train was promised in spring.",
